title: Shore
---
It was a day like any other, summer’s coming to an end.
<<play_sfx "blabla">>
I was on my way to buy a can of beer to enjoy for myself in the evening.
People going around, twisted in their busy schedules, without a moment to stop.
Finally, I entered the grocery store. It seems kind of empty.
<<next_scene>>
While making my way towards the refrigerators, I was thinking where should I go today.
A lot of places came to mind, but only one made sense.
My hand reached out to take a can, deciding which one. I’ll take the usual, maybe.
Back to the cashier. He was a cool guy, younger than me, but still nice to talk to sometimes.
Cashier: “Hey, good to see you again! How’s your day been going?”
You: “...Slightly better now, I guess.”
I drop the can with a slight hit on the table
Cashier: “So, when does your vacation start?”
You: “...Huh?”
Cashier: “The vacation you told me about like, a month ago?”
You: “Oh, that.”
I totally forgot about that...
You: “Actually, it starts today.”
Cashier: “Really? Oh, congratulations!”
You: “Thanks...”
Cashier: “5 dollars for the beer by the way.”
I quickly search my pockets and find a 100-dollar bill.
After a while, the guy hands me spare change, but...
You: “No need to, keep it for yourself. I mean it.”
Cashier: “Sir, I canno-“
You: “I said keep it, okay? That’s my way of repaying you for our small talks this whole time.”
He sighs, nodding, putting it away somewhere on his counter.
I make my way out of the store, towards the place I had in mind, by foot.
And after a while...
<<next_scene>>
Here I am again. At the shore.
I can hear how waves crash in the distance.
I can sense the scent of salt in the air.
I can feel how light breeze touches the fabric.
I stand still, heart stopped for a moment.
But my tired body is wimping for me to sit down.
<<next_scene>>
After carefully swinging my legs down the edge, I open the can.
The first sip feels as refreshing as ever. It always was.
Ocean. It looks as if there is nothing past the horizon.
It’s just me, with infinite allure of the water.
I breath in. Lavender.
Her favorite.
She told me once that this is her secret spot.
She came here every weekends to just gaze into the distance. To count stars. To feel how fresh grass tickled her skin.
Wish I was there with her.
Wish I knew her sooner.
With another inhale – I close my eyes.
I can feel her near me.
<<next_music>>
I can feel how she hugs me one more time.
<<next_scene>>
Her: “Hey...”
You: Hey.
Her: “Long time no see.”
You: Yeah...
Her: “Been doing great?”
You: Not really...
Her: “Oh? Why so?”
You: I miss you.
Her: “I miss you too, sweetheart.”
She gently kisses me in the head.
Her: “Was it hard for you?”
You: Immensely.
Her: “But  I... hoped it was for the better.”
You: It never got better. It only got worse.
Her: “Why?...”
You: Well, I don’t really know.
You: It is hard to... move on.
Her: “I was praying for you to be happy.”
You: I will never be happy again.
Her: “Oh, silly...”
You: No, I’m serious.
You: I will never find happiness again.
Her: “...”
You: It’s been very harsh these past few months.
You: I hoped it would become better, but...
Her: “...Don’t lose hope yet.”
You: Can I?
You: I’ve been thinking about today for a while now.
You: I’ve even gave our cat to the friend of ours.
Her: “...”
You: ...
You: Can you do one more thing for me?
Her: “...Of course.”
You: Tell me that we’ll see each other. Again. Once more.
Her: “...”
Her: “I promise.”
You: Thank you.
My body suddenly became limp.
It doesn’t obey me no more.
I see how the water becomes closer.
I close my eyes.
...
===
